  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal legal and business term. Unlike {解雇|かいこ} (firing an employee), {解任|かいにん} specifically refers to removing someone from an appointed position or office, such as a company officer, director, or official.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {解任|かいにん}する (to dismiss from office)\n- {解任|かいにん}される (to be dismissed from office)\n- {解任|かいにん}{動議|どうぎ} (motion for dismissal)\n- {解任|かいにん}{決議|けつぎ} (resolution for dismissal)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {解雇|かいこ}: firing, dismissal — for regular employees\n- {罷免|ひめん}: removal from office — stronger, more formal, often for public officials\n- {更迭|こうてつ}: replacement, reshuffle — replacing someone in a position",
